<h2>Approval and purchase are separate</h2>
<p>Saving an approval records a limit and a reason. It never buys anything. Sponsored spending happens only through Buy renewal with reseller funds, or through the daily billing run for an approval that covers every future renewal.</p>
<p>Both need the Authorize Enom sponsorship permission and the domain's renewal policy set to On. A zero retail price on its own allows no spending.</p>
<h2>This renewal only</h2>
<p>The approval covers only the expiry the domain had when it was saved. A staff member must still use Buy renewal with reseller funds. The daily billing run does not act on this kind of approval.</p>
<p>Once that renewal succeeds, the expiry moves forward and the approval no longer covers the domain. The page then shows no approval for the current cycle, and the buy action is not offered until a new approval is saved.</p>
<h2>Every future renewal</h2>
<p>This is a standing approval. From the review start day of each cycle, the daily billing run can request a renewal when its quote is within the approved limit, without another click. The review start day is the issue-day setting counted back from the confirmed expiry. No customer invoice is issued and there is no due date.</p>
<p>This needs the renewal policy On for the domain, Schedule domain renewal invoices and Allow registrar changes on for the server, and an eligible domain.</p>
<h2>The limit and the final charge</h2>
<p>The limit applies to the accepted registrar quote. It is checked when the request is created and again just before it is sent. The final Enom charge is not capped and can differ from the quote.</p>
<p>A confirmed charge above the approved limit pauses further automatic spending for the domain.</p>
<h2>What a purchase checks</h2>
<ul class="enom-list space-y-1">
    <li>An approval that covers the current expiry, with a USD limit and a one-year term.</li>
    <li>A managed domain with a zero retail price, the renewal policy On, an active service, no cancellation and no open request.</li>
    <li>A complete registrar quote from the last 15 minutes, at or under the limit. The buy action reads a fresh quote first.</li>
    <li>Automatic spending is not paused for the domain.</li>
</ul>
<p>A repeat purchase request for the same expiry returns the existing request. It does not create a second one.</p>
<h2>Withdrawing</h2>
<p>Withdrawing stops spending under the approval, including a queued request that has not been sent. A request that was already sent still needs registrar review.</p>
<p>Choosing Not approved in the approval form still asks for a limit and reason, but a withdrawal does not save them. When the approval covers the current expiry, Withdraw approval needs only a confirmation.</p>
